-- check/bad: a SATURATED operator section is the operator call it stands
-- for (§3.1), so it is a `method_call` and `not_equatable` is reported at
-- the OPERATOR, which is what §10.3 requires of every well-known call: "the
-- `.m` token for a dot-call; the operator token for `<` and friends".
-- `(==) inc inc` underlines `(==)` at 13:6 — not the first operand, a
-- token the author did not write the mistake at.
--
pub inc : Int → Int
inc n = n


pub bad : Bool
bad = (==) inc inc
